Die Alte
W. A. Mozart (1756–1791)
KV 517
Gedicht von Friedr. von Hagedorn
Voice and Piano
18th May 1787
Classical


Breitkopf &amp; Härtel (serie 7 n. 26)
Public Domain
Mutopia-2005/12/09-343
Maurizio Tomasi
zio_tom78@hotmail.com
http://www.geocities.com/zio_tom78/
<p><b>Die Alte (The old lady)</b></p><p>This Lied was composed by Mozart in 1787, the year of Don Giovanni and Eine Kleine Nachtmusick, but also the great year of Lieder. It is a sort of "musical joke": an old lady mourns the old days of her youth, when things went better. The musical style too tries to evoke those "old days", as the chords in the piano part recall an old-fashoned harpsichord.</p>
2.6.4


