<p>The Breitkopf &amp; Haertel edition used as the source was published in 1877, edited by Johannes Brahms (1833-1897).</p><p>It is also called the &quot;Süssmayr&quot; version, because Franz Xaver Süssmayr (1766-1803) took credit for completing the Requiem after Mozart's death. There is much rumor as to who else was involved.</p>
